# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# READ FIRST — this file is currently INERT in production.
#
# The Sites host that serves lumii.com.au (see .openai/hosting.json) does not
# process `_redirects` (nor `_headers`). Verified 2026-08-02: the Astro-generated
# `/ → /en-au/ 301` rule was present in dist/client/_redirects and the root still
# returned 404. Anything that MUST work in production has to be a real emitted
# asset, not a rule in here. The rules below are kept because they are correct
# and cost nothing — they start working the day the project moves to Cloudflare
# Pages / Workers static assets, which do honour this file.
#
# www → apex (lumii.com.au) is an EDGE redirect (Cloudflare Redirect Rule), not a
# file rule: static-assets `_redirects` rejects absolute URLs ("Only relative
# URLs are allowed"), and host-to-host belongs at the edge anyway. See README
# "Needs Garth → Cloudflare → custom domains".
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The default locale (en-au) is unprefixed and owns the site root, so the old
# prefixed URLs are legacy. Keep these until nothing links to /en-au/… any more:
# the site was briefly live on that shape, so external links and any indexed URL
# should land on the canonical page rather than the 404.
/en-au/          /              301
/en-au/*         /:splat        301

# Add only RELATIVE, in-site path redirects below (e.g. /old-path /new-path 301).
